as we all know the new 14 and 16 inch  macbook pros come with new mini led  displays that can get insanely bright  while also having incredibly dark levels  of contrast but if the display isn't  pointed directly at you then the  blooming becomes noticeable and it's  actually quite distracting and the thing  i didn't expect was that i would notice  the blooming in shots that are more  dimly lit and hazy like many of the  shots from the movie dune and it just  gets so much worse when you're viewing  it from the side and especially if your  eyes are looking down at the display the  viewing angles in general aren't as good  as they were before causing the display  to look a bit dimmer from the side and  the top i actually have to be  intentional about how i place my macbook  pro when watching something to avoid  blooming which is a bit disappointing  but the display still looks so much  better than the previous ones so it's  still worth it when you're looking  straight at it there are no issues at  all and most people likely won't even  notice when looking from the side
 

